### Steps to reproduce

I ran into this while working on a UI with many widgets kept mounted. Camera movement became much more expensive when semantics was enabled.

Turning semantics off globally removed most of that cost, but wrapping the entire workspace in ExcludeSemantics didn't. I expected the excluded content to stop contributing to semantics processing, so I looked into where the time was going.

The recurring work comes from the deferred geometry handling added in [#192146](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/pull/192146). Render objects that are excluded or blocked stay in a deferred set. On every semantics flush, Flutter takes them out, checks whether they can be processed, and puts them back if their branch is still excluded.

That keeps happening even when the children haven't changed and will remain excluded indefinitely.

### Expected results

The excluded children keep adding work to each semantics flush. The cost grows with the size of the excluded subtree. I also reproduced the same queue behavior with BlockSemantics.

In a separate release/AOT microbenchmark on macOS, 10,000 excluded annotated children added about 1.15 ms per flush even after the branch had settled. This measures the semantics queue directly, not the frame time of the sample above.

### Actual results

Pending geometry updates should be remembered while a subtree is excluded and applied when it rejoins the semantics tree, without retrying all those objects on every frame.

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

Run this code on MacOS with: `flutter run --profile -d macos --dart-define=NODES=10000`

Record the UI timeline after startup and look at SEMANTICS and Semantics.ensureGeometry. Then try `--dart-define=NODES=100` and compare the time spent there.

The children stay mounted throughout the animation. Only their ancestor's transform changes.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';

const int nodeCount = int.fromEnvironment(
  'NODES',
  defaultValue: 10000,
);

void main() {
  final binding = WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  binding.ensureSemantics();

  runApp(
    const Directionality(
      textDirection: TextDirection.ltr,
      child: Repro(),
    ),
  );
}

class Repro extends StatefulWidget {
  const Repro({super.key});

  @override
  State<Repro> createState() => _ReproState();
}

class _ReproState extends State<Repro>
    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late final AnimationController controller = AnimationController(
    vsync: this,
    duration: const Duration(seconds: 1),
  )..repeat(reverse: true);

  @override
  void dispose() {
    controller.dispose();
    super.dispose();
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Column(
      children: <Widget>[
        Text('Semantics enabled; $nodeCount excluded children.'),
        AnimatedBuilder(
          animation: controller,
          builder: (BuildContext context, Widget? child) {
            return Transform.translate(
              offset: Offset(controller.value * 10, 0),
              child: child,
            );
          },
          child: ExcludeSemantics(
            child: Wrap(
              children: List<Widget>.generate(
                nodeCount,
                (int i) => Semantics(
                  label: 'Node $i',
                  child: const SizedBox(width: 2, height: 2),
                ),
              ),
            ),
          ),
        ),
      ],
    );
  }
}```

